n China\n\nChina rose 2.9%, USD 2,420/MT to USD 2,490/MT. Export prices recovered off their 2025 lows and ilmenite firmed, but with capacity everywhere, China stayed the cheapest source.\n\nWhy did the price of Titanium Dioxide change in Q2 2026 in China?\n\nExport quotes came up off the floor. Ilmenite cost more. Even so, the country's capacity kept prices the lowest on the panel.\n\n### Titanium Dioxide Prices in Germany\n\nGermany moved the most, 3.1% to USD 3,650/MT from USD 3,540/MT, and stayed dearest. Anti-dumping duties on Chinese imports and energy-heavy sulphate-route costs kept it there.\n\nWhy did the price of Titanium Dioxide change in Q2 2026 in Germany?\n\nThe duties took the cheapest imports out of contention. Energy-heavy processing and dearer ore did the rest, holding a high floor.\n\n### Titanium Dioxide Prices in India\n\nIndia rose 2.8%, USD 2,880/MT to USD 2,960/MT. Recovering coatings and construction demand met firmer imported feedstock.\n\nWhy did the price of Titanium Dioxide change in Q2 2026 in India?\n\nCoatings and construction picked back up. Imported ilmenite and rutile firmed, and the wave of producer increases reached India too.\n\n### For the Quarter Ending March 2026\n\n#### Titanium Dioxide Prices Q1 2026:\n\n  * United States: USD 3,180/MT\n  * China: USD 2,420/MT\n  * Germany: USD 3,540/MT\n  * India: USD 2,880/MT\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProduct Details (https://www.spectrumchemical.com/pdfdetails/pdf/index/productSku/T1081/)\nciteturn18search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 months ago; Titanium Dioxide, Technical, is the naturally available oxide of titanium also known as ... pure titanium, electrical ceramics, catalysts and other chemical applications.\nProduct Details\nWWW.SPECTRUMCHEMICAL.COM\nTitanium Dioxide, Technical\nSDS\nItem Number CAS Number | T1081 13463-67-7 --- | --- Item Number Molecular Formula | T1081 TiO 2 Item Number Molecular Weight | T1081 79.87